---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Cite from '../../components/Cite.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/url';
---
<Layout title="For issuers" description="Reach verified investors across borders without rebuilding onboarding, and preview the effect of every distribution policy change before you publish it." path="solutions/issuers/">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Your fund is tokenized. Now let it reach investors abroad.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Asset managers and fund administrators use Laissez to open a tokenized fund to distributors in new jurisdictions. Your token, registry, transfer agent and chain stay exactly as they are.</p>
      <div class="hero-cta"><a class="btn primary" href={url('app/')}>Try the sandbox</a><a class="arrow-link" href={url('demo/')}>See the issuer view</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band light">
    <div class="wrap cols-2">
      <div><h2>Issuance scaled. Reach did not.</h2></div>
      <div>
        <p class="lede">Tokenized U.S. Treasury funds hold $14.69B across 108 products.<Cite id="rwa-treasuries" /> Yet the largest have only dozens to low hundreds of holders: 104 for BUIDL and 46 for iBENJI.<Cite id={['rwa-buidl', 'rwa-ibenji']} /> High minimums explain part of that. The rest is distribution: every new country and every new distributor means new eligibility work.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><h2>Set the policy once. Laissez enforces it everywhere the fund is sold.</h2></div>
      <div class="cols-3">
        <div class="item"><span class="k">Reach</span><h4>Investors already verified</h4><p>Every distributor on the network brings credentialed investors. Opening a jurisdiction opens it to all of them on day one.</p></div>
        <div class="item"><span class="k">Control</span><h4>Your distribution policy, machine-enforced</h4><p>Choose jurisdictions, investor classes, minimums, holder caps, lock-ups and accepted cash assets. Laissez checks them on every subscription and transfer.</p></div>
        <div class="item"><span class="k">Change</span><h4>Impact before you publish</h4><p>Remove a jurisdiction and see how many holders and how much value move to redemption-only before the change goes live. Nobody is force-redeemed.</p></div>
        <div class="item"><span class="k">Stack</span><h4>Nothing to replace</h4><p>Add Laissez as a trusted claim issuer in your ERC-3643 identity registry. Your transfer agent remains the register of record.</p></div>
        <div class="item"><span class="k">Governance</span><h4>Two keys on every change</h4><p>Policy changes require a second approver. Rule packs change only with counsel sign-off.</p></div>
        <div class="item"><span class="k">Cost</span><h4>Free for issuers in the pilot</h4><p>Distributors pay for the platform. Issuers integrate at no charge so more funds reach more investors.</p></div>
        <div class="item"><span class="k">Fund operations</span><h4>NAV, accruals, documents, notices</h4><p>Strike a NAV, run accruals and distributions, publish offering documents at a version investors acknowledge, and receive redemption notices against the fund’s dealing calendar.</p></div>
        <div class="item"><span class="k">On-chain</span><h4>Your ERC-3643 token, reconciled</h4><p>Settlement writes to your token on your chain and reconciles balances against the register. Base Sepolia testnet contracts are built; the deployment is pending.</p></div>
        <div class="item"><span class="k">Reports</span><h4>Placement and distribution reports</h4><p>Who holds what, where, under which rule pack version, exportable as CSV for your administrator and regulator.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band cta-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Open a sandbox as the issuer.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Switch to the issuer admin teammate, change a fund’s distribution list and watch the impact preview before you publish.</p>
      <div class="hero-cta"><a class="btn primary" href={url('app/')}>Try the sandbox</a><a class="arrow-link" href={url('access/')}>Talk to us about a pilot</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
<style>
  .cta-band .hero-cta { display: flex; gap: 1.25rem; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.75rem; }
</style>
